# Changelog

All notable changes to all gonemaster components will be documented in this file.

## [Unreleased]

Gives the server structured text or json logging with per-request IDs and one access-log line per request. Rebuilds snapshots in the background with a progress bar. Adds glossary tooltips to public finding explanations and completes the result explanations across every shipped locale.

### Added

- ui-public: a DNS glossary linking jargon in finding explanations to plain-language tooltips, in every shipped locale
- ui-public: finding and testcase explanations translated into Danish, Norwegian Bokmal, Spanish, Finnish, and Slovenian
- ui-public: DS10 non-standard-NSEC tag explanation and the ZONEMD apex testcase name in the remaining locales
- admin-ui, server: a progress bar while a snapshot is rebuilt; the rebuild runs in the background instead of freezing the button
- admin-ui: sortable columns on the snapshot table
- server: text or json logs, set with `--log-format` and `--log-level`
- server: a request ID on each API request, returned as `X-Request-Id` and shown in the logs
- server: one access-log line per API request

### Changed

- server: server logs now use a structured logger; `--debug` logs request and response bodies

### Fixed

- admin-ui, server: rebuilding a snapshot no longer changes its captured date, so the snapshot list stays newest-first

## [v1.6.2] - 2026-07-16

Reworks the public analysis dashboards: a stat-tile overview, a focus mode and top movers in trends, a richer snapshot diff, latency and history on entity pages, keyboard shortcuts, and honest exports. Adds a one-click way to run a cohort snapshot and make it the default, and updates the bundled DNS library.

### Added

- analysis-ui: the overview leads with stat tiles (domains, share without warnings, grade A/A+, signed) that show the change since the previous snapshot and a sparkline, plus a since-last-snapshot movers card and the leading provider's share on the infrastructure cards
- analysis-ui: trends focus mode - click a legend bucket to pin its share or count as a line across snapshots - plus a top-movers panel and CSV export of the visible series
- analysis-ui: snapshot diff summary strip, grade-transition matrix, directional grade rows, linked domains, a swap-sides button, and CSV export
- analysis-ui, server: tag-level snapshot diff showing which finding tags appeared, cleared, or changed severity cohort-wide
- analysis-ui, server: p50/p95 latency on the nameserver, address, and ASN lists and detail pages, from queries the snapshot already recorded
- analysis-ui, server: per-entity history sparklines on the nameserver, ASN, tag, and domain detail pages
- analysis-ui: keyboard shortcuts - g then a letter to jump between sections, / to focus search, ? for a help overlay
- analysis-ui: a top navigation progress bar during blocking loads, and a restored prefixes list page
- admin-ui, server: a "Run + set as default" option next to "Run new snapshot" on the cohorts page - it runs a snapshot and pins it as the cohort's default as soon as it finishes capturing

### Changed

- analysis-ui: exports cover the whole filtered set (up to the 500-row server limit) and state the row count, instead of only the rows on screen
- analysis-ui: shared empty-state styling, accessible distribution bars (screen-reader counts, ellipsis on squeezed segments), and grade/severity colours moved to themeable tokens with dark-mode fixes
- server: revalidate analysis snapshot responses with ETags instead of marking them immutable
- server, engine: update the bundled DNS library (miekg/dns) to v0.6.84

### Fixed

- analysis, server: per-address ASN and prefix enrichment failed without its nameserver cache, leaving ASN rosters and the prefix count empty; the cache is now attached and the results cached

## [v1.6.1] - 2026-07-14

Stops reporting a false DNSSEC failure on zones signed with an RSA key whose public exponent is too large for the local verifier (for example the `.lv` TLD). Adds structured data and social image metadata to the public result page.

### Added

- engine, docs: NOTICE tags `DS02_RSA_EXPONENT_UNSUPPORTED`, `DS08_RSA_EXPONENT_UNSUPPORTED`, and `DS09_RSA_EXPONENT_UNSUPPORTED`, translated into every shipped locale
- ui-public: JSON-LD structured data on the result page, with Open Graph, Twitter, and JSON-LD image URLs built on the public origin

### Changed

- server: sync the public UI hreflang languages with the shipped locales

### Fixed

- engine: reclassify DNSSEC02/08/09 RRSIG failures caused only by an RSA public exponent the local verifier cannot use as unverifiable, not invalid; no `*_RRSIG_NOT_VALID_BY_DNSKEY` error and no grade impact

## [v1.6.0] - 2026-07-12

Reports a stale DS at the parent of an unsigned zone as an error. Adds a DNSSEC chain-of-trust graph to the public result page. Adds SEO metadata to the analysis dashboards. Flags timed-out name servers as unreachable.

### Added

- engine, server: build a DNSSEC chain-of-trust summary for each run from the queries it already makes (no extra lookups, public-UI runs only), with the keys, DS records, and signatures that link a zone to its parent, gated by `show_dnssec_chain_public`. Older and non-public runs have no chain data.
- ui-public: draw that summary as a small chain-of-trust graph on the public result page, with the keys and DS records coloured by whether their signatures are valid, a status badge, and hover details in every language.
- analysis-ui, server: SEO and social metadata for the analysis dashboards - per-route titles, descriptions and canonical URLs, Open Graph and Twitter cards, a favicon, and the dashboard pages listed in `sitemap.xml`
- engine, admin-ui: track query timeouts separately from response times and surface unreachable/unresolved name servers in the timing view
- docs, analysis-ui: zone14 and dnssec21 testcase titles and a zone14 result explanation

### Changed

- engine: run dnssec11 for unsigned zones so a stale DS still published at the parent is reported as an error (`DS11_DS_BUT_UNSIGNED_ZONE`) instead of being hidden by the `DS07_NOT_SIGNED` short-circuit
- server: report a timed-out name server as unreachable in the timing summary

### Fixed

- engine: register zone13 in the zone testcase map so it actually runs; it was implemented but never dispatched
- engine: initialize `queryTimeouts` in `SnapshotForRun` to prevent a nil-map panic on server runs

## [v1.5.9] - 2026-07-09

Reworks the admin UI with hash-based deep links, a batches list/detail view, global keyboard shortcuts, unified result rendering, and shared notice/confirm dialogs. Nameserver01 now requires RA=1 before flagging NXDOMAIN-only servers as recursors.

### Added

- admin-ui: hash router with deep links for tabs, settings, jobs, domains, tags, and batches that survive reload and open in new tabs
- admin-ui: batches list/detail view at `#/batches/<id>` with clickable job rows showing severity pills and grade
- admin-ui: global keyboard shortcuts with a help overlay, translated into all catalogs
- admin-ui: dirty-state guard that warns before discarding unsaved settings edits
- admin-ui: roving arrow-key navigation in the settings tablist

### Changed

- engine: nameserver01 requires RA=1 to flag NXDOMAIN-only servers as recursors
- admin-ui: unify result rendering into RunResultView with shared ScoreCard and GradeChip
- admin-ui: consolidate feedback onto a shared InlineNotice and tiered ConfirmDialog confirmations, render timestamps ISO-style, and move the severity palette to CSS vars
- admin-ui: lay out the batch create form and batches list side-by-side
- server, admin-ui: make severity filtering server-authoritative and drop the client re-filter
- docs: restructure README with quick start, releases, nagios/MCP, and license

### Fixed

- admin-ui: fix ReferenceError on batch load from stale recentBatchOptions
- admin-ui: fix dark-theme modal colors and the empty worst-level badge class
- admin-ui: fix wrong-key error messages and distinguish tag load-error from empty

## [v1.5.8] - 2026-07-06

Adds a tag run-purge endpoint and admin UI action, plus AXFR zone-transfer caching in the packet cache with new `--cache-stats` and `--cache-strict` CLI flags. Adopts RFC 9499 "in-domain" terminology in place of "bailiwick". Reworks Zone09 MX consistency reporting and renames nameserver15 to software version disclosure.

### Added

- server: add `POST /api/v1/tags/{name}/purge` to delete all completed runs and entries for a tag while leaving active jobs, tag memberships, and captured cohort snapshots intact
- admin-ui: add a tag detail "Purge runs" action with two-step confirmation
- engine: cache and replay AXFR zone transfers per run and persist AXFR entries in the packet cache file
- gonemaster: add `--cache-stats` to print statistics for a saved cache file, `--cache-strict` to treat cache-file warnings as errors, and a restored-run cache hit/miss summary

### Changed

- server: refuse `DELETE /api/v1/tags/{name}` with `409` while an analysis cohort is built on the tag
- engine, i18n, docs: adopt RFC 9499 "in-domain" terminology in place of "bailiwick" in log messages and documentation
- zone09: compare MX records by RDATA and report inconsistent MX by name server host name; reword `Z09_INCONSISTENT_MX_DATA`
- zone09: `Z09_NON_AUTH_MX_RESPONSE` now reports the IP addresses of the non-authoritative responders
- nameserver15: rename testcase to "software version disclosure" and clarify its software-version log messages across the engine, admin-ui, ui-public, and analysis-ui
- admin-ui: convert `App.svelte` to Svelte 5 runes mode

## [v1.5.7] - 2026-06-30

Adds Czech (cs) and Dutch (nl) locales. Removes the deprecated resolver profile properties `igntc`, `recurse`, and `usevc`. Nameserver15 escapes unprintable bytes in reported software-version strings.

### Added

- i18n: add Czech (cs) engine message catalog and locale across admin-ui and ui-public
- i18n: add Dutch (nl) engine message catalog and locale across admin-ui and ui-public

### Changed

- engine: remove deprecated resolver profile properties `igntc`, `recurse`, and `usevc`; stored profiles carrying them load without error and the keys are ignored
- docs: refresh dnssec10 and nameserver test specifications and the upstream-divergence notes after upstream comparison; mark the nameserver13 query-type and recursor cache-context divergences resolved

### Fixed

- nameserver15: escape unprintable bytes in software-version strings before logging so control characters and invalid UTF-8 cannot reach logs or the UIs verbatim
- build: review the `fsevents` install script via `allowScripts` in the UI `package.json` files so `npm install` no longer warns under npm 11.17+

## [v1.5.6] - 2026-06-27

Added Nameserver18 test case for Extended DNS Errors (EDE, RFC 8914), reported as score-neutral diagnostics. The admin UI can now pull new default scoring entries into a saved configuration. Some engine and server fixes.

### Added

- engine: add nameserver18 Extended DNS Errors (EDE, RFC 8914) testcase
- nameserver18: classify observed EDE codes into server-error, resolver-behavior, filtered, and benign findings
- nameserver18: add spec, tag catalog, zero-penalty scoring defaults, and i18n strings
- admin-ui, ui-public, analysis-ui: add nameserver18 Extended DNS Errors testcase title and tag explanations
- admin-ui: add default scoring entries missing from a saved scoring configuration (e.g. the new N18 tag penalties)

### Changed

- server: gate profile compatibility on schema_version so mark-as-reviewed clears the warning
- engine: render opaque NSID as dig-style hex so bytes survive JSON (fixes #87)

## [v1.5.5] - 2026-06-24

New non-global query guard skips queries to private/special-use nameserver addresses by default and tags them `NON_GLOBAL_QUERY_BLOCKED`. Private/internal deployments must opt in via `net.allow_non_global_targets` (profile), `--allow-non-global` (CLI/Nagios), or the admin UI toggle. Several test case improvements: zone10 apex CNAME/DNAME detection, delegation01 missing in-bailiwick glue, consistency01/04 SOA and NS TTL consistency, and basic01 DNAME alias handling.

### Added

- engine: non-global query guard - skip queries to private/special-use NS addresses by default; `net.allow_non_global_targets` profile flag, `--allow-non-global` CLI/Nagios flag, admin-ui policy toggle, and server public-api policy clamp to opt in
- zone10: detect CNAME at apex (SOA_AND_CNAME, ERROR) and DNAME at apex (APEX_DNAME, NOTICE)
- basic01: suppress B01_NO_CHILD for DNAME alias targets, add IsDNAMEAlias
- delegation01: flag in-bailiwick NS names with missing required glue (IN_BAILIWICK_GLUE_MISSING)
- consistency04: flag inconsistent apex NS RRset TTLs across nameservers
- consistency01: RFC 1982 SOA serial ordering and lagging server reporting
- scoring: lock system module tags as score-neutral

### Changed

- server: batch purge uses batched deletes to avoid InnoDB lock wait timeouts
- deps: bump npm dependencies to fix high-severity vulnerabilities

