## [v1.4.3] - 2026-05-01

Fixed a lot of public-ui security related things.

### Security
 - server: refuse undelegated nameserver IPs in loopback / link-local / private / CGNAT / multicast / broadcast ranges on the public API (override with `--public-api-allow-private-undelegated-ip` for private/internal deployments)
 - server: enforce CSRF Origin check on `POST /pub/api/v1/jobs`
 - server: cache `GET /pub/api/v1/jobs/{id}/result` for 5 min so a CDN/reverse proxy absorbs repeat reads
 - server: cap connection wall time with `--read-timeout` 30s / `--write-timeout` 60s / `--idle-timeout` 60s (slowloris)
 - admin-ui: add 'No tag' filter option to domains tab tag dropdown

### Changed
 - server: `X-Forwarded-For` is no longer trusted by default. Set `--trusted-proxy-cidrs` (or `trusted_proxy_cidrs` in the config file) to the CIDR of your reverse proxy. Without it, requests are attributed to `RemoteAddr`. **Breaking** for deployments behind a reverse proxy that previously relied on automatic XFF parsing.
 - server: `X-Real-IP` is no longer honoured. Use `X-Forwarded-For` (which Caddy and the documented nginx example already set).
 - server: CSRF check now also honors `X-Forwarded-Proto` from trusted proxies, so `POST /pub/api/v1/jobs` works behind TLS-terminating reverse proxies. **Set `trusted_proxy_cidrs` to the proxy's IP** or browsers see 403 `csrf_origin_mismatch`.
 - analysis-ui: endpointHref replaces stale nameserver= so chip clicks don't 404

