 - UI: Recent test rows are now fully clickable in the Admin UI
 - Engine: Bumped miekg/dns to v0.6.73
 - Engine: Nameserver01 fixed for false positive for some cases of open recursor

## [v1.2.2] - 2026-03-30

### Added
 - gonemaster-nagios: `--ns` and `--ds` flags for undelegated/split-DNS testing
 - gonemaster-nagios: `--rrsig-warn-days` flag to warn when apex RRSIG expires within N days

 ### Changed
 - engine: Recover from DNS library panic in verifyRRSIG on oversized RRsets

## [v1.2.1] - 2026-03-29

### Added
 - Server: security headers middleware sets `X-Content-Type-Options`, `X-Frame-Options`, `Content-Security-Policy`, `Referrer-Policy`, and `Permissions-Policy` on all responses
 - Server: Two-tier queue priority - `POST /jobs` submits at priority 0 (normal, for single jobs and the public ui), `POST /jobs/batch` at priority 1 (batch); normal always drains first
 - UI: Added logotype and favicon
 - UI: Added more security headers

## [v1.2.0] - 2026-03-26

**Major changes:**
  - New simple UI for end-users
  - Database persistence with support for PostgreSQL, and MariaDB/MySQL
  - Domain registry with tags, run history, and per-entry SQL analysis

### Added

 - Server: Domain registry - completed jobs graduate to persistent `domains` + `runs` + `entries` records; all three are queryable via the admin API and directly via SQL
 - Server: Tags - named domain collections; `POST/GET /api/v1/tags`, `PUT/DELETE /api/v1/tags/{name}`, `POST/GET/DELETE /api/v1/tags/{name}/domains`, `GET /api/v1/tags/{name}/summary`
 - Server: Domains API - `GET /api/v1/domains`, `GET /api/v1/domains/{id}`, `GET /api/v1/domains/{id}/runs`; filter by tag, name, level, min_level
 - Server: Runs API - `GET /api/v1/runs`, `GET /api/v1/runs/{id}`, `GET /api/v1/runs/{id}/result`; filter by tag, domain, batch, status, level, time range
 - Server: Entries API - `GET /api/v1/entries` with filters for run, domain, tag, module, testcase, entry tag, level, latest-per-domain, batch; CSV export via `?format=csv`
 - Server: Batch `POST /api/v1/jobs/batch` now accepts `from_tag` (re-run all domains in a tag), `tags` (tag all created domains), and `description` fields
 - Server: SQLite, PostgreSQL, and MariaDB/MySQL persistence backends with versioned schema migrations, startup recovery, and integration tests (`make test-integration`)
 - Server: `--db-driver` / `--db-dsn` / `GONEMASTER_DB_*` env vars and JSON config file support
 - Server: Data retention - `--db-retention-days` runs hourly background purge; `POST /api/v1/jobs/purge` and `gonemaster-client jobs purge` for on-demand purging
 - Docs: `docs/data-analysis.md` - end-to-end guide for bulk analysis: backend selection, tag/batch workflows, API queries, direct SQL examples, CSV export, and deployment patterns
 - Server: Public API at `/pub/api/v1/` - job submission and result lookup by short public ID, without leaking internal UUIDs; per-IP sliding-window rate limiting with `429`/`Retry-After`
 - Server: Version endpoint at `/pub/api/v1/version` returning gonemaster and miekg/dns versions
 - Admin UI: Domains tab - browse/filter the domain registry, drill into per-domain run history
 - Admin UI: Tags tab - create/edit/delete tags, manage domain membership, per-tag severity summary
 - Admin UI: Run inspector - shows duration, entry count, and worst level; domain name is a clickable link to the Domains tab; batch re-run support
 - Admin UI: i18n - 75 new translation keys across 9 languages for all new UI sections
 - Public UI: Svelte SPA at `/public/` - domain testing without admin access; user config IPv4/IPv6 transport, undelegated NS/DS input, shareable result URLs, and 9 languages
 - Public UI: Test results grouped by test case with translated descriptions; auto-expand for warnings/errors; severity badges per group
 - Public UI: NS/DS lookup and fetch-from-parent buttons; DS algo/digest-type dropdowns with IANA values; reset button; striped progress bar; version footer
 - Admin UI: Job inspector shows test case sub-groups within modules, translated descriptions, auto-expand for warnings/errors, and an overall status banner
 - Client: `domains` command group - `list`, `get`, `runs`, `tag`, `untag`
 - Client: `tags` command group - `list`, `create`, `delete`, `domains`, `summary`, `add-domains`
 - Client: `runs` command group - `list`, `get`, `results`
 - Client: `entries` command group - `query` (with CSV export via `--format csv`)
 - Client: `jobs batch` - new `--from-tag` (re-run all domains in a tag) and `--tag` (apply tag to batch) flags
 - Engine: INFO-level success tags for DNSSEC02/06/08/09/11/13/18 (all-algorithms-signed, parent-DS-consistent, valid-RRSIGs, etc.)
 - Engine: CN01_OK_UDP and CN02_OK_TCP summary INFO tags for passing connectivity tests

### Changed

 - Server: Job results are now assembled from `runs` + `entries` tables; the old `results` table and `result_url` field are removed
 - SQL layer refactored for multi-dialect support
 - Engine: Fixed delegation04/06 success tags suppressed by transport-disabled entries
 - Public UI: Fixed DS lookup to try next resolver on empty answer
 - Public UI: Fixed TLD lookup to use FQDN and wire DNS with public resolver fallbacks
 - UI translations: corrected nameserver08/09 test case labels across all 9 languages; fixed "lim"→"glue" and "lösas upp"→"slås upp" in Nordic translations
 - Engine: Always include System module with version entry first in results
 - Bumped versions on dependencies (miekg/dns 0.6.70 etc.)
 - Normalize domain names to lowercase ACE in GetOrCreateDomain
 - Engine: Skip dead delegation servers and break early in getIBAddrInZone

